.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B duscope
Scan the current directory and draw its treemap.
.TP
.B duscope top ~ \-\-depth 2 \-\-limit 10
The ten largest directories two levels under the home folder.
.TP
.B duscope stale ~/Downloads \-\-older\-than 180d \-\-min\-size 100M
Large downloads nobody has changed for half a year.
.TP
.B duscope by\-type . \-\-examples 3
Bytes by file class, with the three largest files of each.
.TP
.B duscope scan ~ \-\-exclude\-caches \-\-json
The JSON envelope of a scan that leaves out regenerable caches.
.TP
.B duscope scans
The saved scans, newest first: each scan's id, start, entries, sizes and root.
.TP
.B duscope explain ~/dev/app/node_modules
What the directory is, what deleting it would free, and the command that
builds it again.
.TP
.B duscope diff 1fd3 7a2c
What changed between two saved scans of one tree, the largest change first.
.TP
.B duscope query ~ \-\-sql \(dqSELECT path(id), human_size(allocated) FROM files ORDER BY allocated DESC LIMIT 5\(dq
The five largest files, by SQL over the saved scan's tables.
.TP
.B duscope rescan ~/src
Scan the tree a saved scan holds again, with the options it was taken with.
.TP
.B duscope render ~ \-o home.svg
The treemap as an SVG file;
.B \-\-format png
writes a PNG.
.TP
.B duscope export ~ \-\-format ncdu \-o home.json
The scan in ncdu's format, which
.B ncdu \-f home.json
opens and
.B duscope import home.json
reads back.
.TP
.B duscope completions zsh > _duscope
Write the zsh completion script.
